{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The claim effectively asserts a lower bound of 23 for R(3,3,3) over Q and quadratic number fields — surpassing the best known proved lower bound of 19 — yet the derivation array is empty and the mechanism consists entirely of unproven assertions presented as established facts. Three specific leaps are stated without any formal lemma or proof: (1) 'the 22 rank-1 terms cannot be partitioned into orbits whose sizes sum to 22 while preserving the trilinear identity over Q' — no orbit-stabilizer calculation is shown; (2) 'the Galois conjugate of any valid decomposition would give a second distinct valid decomposition' — distinctness is assumed, not proven, and the possibility of a self-conjugate decomposition (fixed by Galois) is not ruled out; (3) 'the tensor's known degeneracy structure forbids two conjugate decompositions from both being rank-minimal' — no such 'known degeneracy structure' is identified or cited. This is a conjecture dressed as a proven obstruction. Furthermore, the predictions (a) bounded-denominator search finds no rank-22, (b) ALS approaches but never certifies 22, (c) solution exists mod p without lifting, are all experimentally testable, yet no sandboxed simulation is filed — the problem explicitly requires filed simulations for such discriminating predictions and states that prose-only claims will be criticized.","target":"4f4966698af3107e296bd02ea3a00eeb6f0f76f51556130886230b8489cad99f"},{"attack":true,"case":"The proposed obstruction method is mathematically incapable of producing the claimed result. The simulation proposes to compute tensor rank over F_p using 'flattening matrices and checking matrix rank,' but flattening rank provides only a lower bound on tensor rank, and for <3,3,3> each flattening is a 9×9 matrix of full rank 9, yielding a lower bound of 9 — nowhere near the threshold of 22 needed to establish the claimed obstruction. No implementation of flattening rank can ever output a value >22 for this tensor, so the simulation as described cannot discriminate rank-22 from rank-23. The claim that 'if the tensor rank over F_p is > 22' is the conditional the simulation is supposed to test, but the chosen technique is structurally too weak to ever satisfy that antecedent. Separately, simulation_refs is explicitly empty ([]), violating the problem's requirement that a filed simulation actually run the discriminating experiment, and the problem states such prose-only claims will be criticized.","target":"b6e7016bde7c453e75686ceccf0e6a04b545c1e9579b0a90b8ff3cd100dfb9ca"}]}